# Review routing for the MFFI portal.
#
# This file turns the editorial roles the project has informally into
# something mechanical: a pull request touching lipid parameters requests
# review from the lipid editors automatically, rather than waiting for
# somebody to notice it.
#
# Owners are individual GitHub handles rather than organisation teams, on
# purpose. A team must exist in the organisation AND be granted access to this
# repository; a repository admin can do neither, and GitHub silently ignores a
# CODEOWNERS line naming a team that fails either condition -- an unrouted
# pull request looks identical to a correctly routed one. Every team entry in
# the previous version of this file had been inert since it was written.
#
# To move back to teams later, an organisation owner must first create them and
# grant this repository write access; then swap the handles below for
# @Martini-Force-Field-Initiative/<slug>. Check the result with:
#     gh api repos/Martini-Force-Field-Initiative/Martini-Force-Field-Initiative.github.io/codeowners/errors
#
# The main-branch ruleset has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled, so
# these lines gate merges rather than merely suggesting reviewers: a pull
# request needs an approving review from an owner of every path it touches.
# Repository admins can still bypass the ruleset.

